{
  "about": "The refusals of an input linked to its producing specification (INPUT-6, INPUT-10, INPUT-11) and of a copy entry (SPEC-9), each reached by the detector that makes it: preparation with the producer a link names, a stored header read against the producer's contract, a layer's own validation, the copy entries of a chain's layers, and a producer read back into a specification being resolved. `consumer`, held at /consumer.yaml, reads the input SRC that its `schema` link /producer.yaml produces. A types entry on a linked input is redundant even when it agrees with the producer, and so is an empty or null types (INPUT-6). Preparation reads no file for link metadata: a linked input without a link, two links for one input, and a link for no linked input are each refused (INPUT-10), as are a link that names the consuming specification, a producer whose selected fields are unlabelled, repeated or undeclared, in selected-field order, and two output contracts under one producer identity. A stored header or a self-describing artifact's typed fields that differ from the producer's output columns mismatch the contract (INPUT-11). producer is the specification the tests linked, which selects ID and VALUE of its three columns. Moved from project_function_invocation.rs at 144fc5559, whose tests compared the fields and context keys each case names, the first finding's by position.",
  "documents": {
    "consumer": {
      "yamaa": "1.0",
      "type": "spec",
      "domain": "TEST",
      "base": "SRC",
      "input": {"SRC": {"path": "produced.csv", "schema": "nested/producer.yaml"}},
      "keys": ["ID"],
      "columns": [{"name": "ID", "type": "int", "derivation": {"value": "SRC.ID"}, "label": "ID"}],
      "output": {"path": "produced.csv", "columns": ["ID"]}
    }
  },
